  "body": "## Cluster C1 \u2013 OpenBao Unseal-Race (rootless-Podman)\n\nAfter a control-plane restart under rootless Podman the OpenBao member rebinds\nits 127.0.0.1:8200 listener late (Raft/storage rejoin behind the PostgreSQL HA\nendpoint). The in-container seal-status probe between Inspect and Unseal\nanswered `connection refused` and the restart flow failed fast\n(runtime_restart_integration_test.go:25).\n\n### Fix\n`probeMemberState` adds **bounded Retry** (retry=true) in the Unseal path\n`unsealAllMembersWithKey`: same 5s per-attempt budget, up to `memberRestartAttempts`\n(5) with 500ms backoff, bounded by the caller context. A member that never\nanswers or exhausts its budget still fails fast. Inspect keeps single-probe.\n\n### Evidence\n- Regression: `TestUnsealConvergesAfterMemberRestartRace` converges after transient\n  member failures; `TestUnsealFailsFastWhenMemberNeverAnswers` preserves fail-fast.\n- `go build/vet`, `internal/openbao` tests green. Podman/telemetry gate failures\n  are pre-existing on base (env-specific), unrelated to this change.\n\nPR against develop, no merge. Evidence: evidence/board-2026-10-22/o89-openbao-retry.md\n",
